Revision history for Net-Flickr-API

{{$NEXT}}
        - a request that timed out is retried, up to three times
        - when Flickr reports the API disabled for too long, api_call logs an
          error and returns undef, instead of calling exit
        - with the XPath handler, a response that isn't XML (like an LWP
          timeout) is a logged failure, instead of a fatal error
        - a Flickr API error (stat="fail") makes api_call return undef, as
          documented, instead of returning the error document
        - XML that isn't a Flickr reply (no stat="ok") makes api_call return
          undef

1.8       2026-09-26 20:52:50-04:00 America/New_York
        - API calls are paced with a token bucket on Time::HiRes, allowing up
          to 3600 per hour; request latency no longer adds to the pause
        - new flickr.api_calls_per_hour option, capped at 3600
        - HTTP 429 is retried as well as 503, honoring Retry-After as seconds
          or a date
        - retries are a loop, not recursion, so nested calls no longer reset
          the retry count
        - giving up on retries returns undef, instead of passing undef to
          parse_api_call

!!! Logs for previous changes are found in Changes.rdf, which may some day be
    rewritten into ... well, something other than RDF.
